{
  "decision": "done",
  "reason": "The fix changes TIMESTAMP from tokens.Keyword to tokens.Name.Builtin, matching DATE and INTERVAL. This allows the TypedLiteral grouping logic in group_typed_literal() to recognize TIMESTAMP as an opening typed literal keyword (via M_OPEN = T.Name.Builtin, None) and group it with the following string literal. This directly addresses all three cases in the bug report: (1) TIMESTAMP '2020-01-01 00:00:00' will now be grouped as one token like DATE, (2) timestamp '2020-01-01' + interval '1 day' will keep timestamp grouped with its string as the left operand, and (3) created > timestamp '2020-01-01 00:00:00' will no longer split the keyword from the string. The fix is minimal and targets the root cause without adding special cases."
}
```

